    "narrative": "The Austin Waves field a high-upside lineup today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.21), who benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Kumar Rocker. With an elite order slot and a +14% platoon adjustment, **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary engine for power and run production. Joining him in the elite tier are **Kyle Tucker** (75.28), **Andy Pages** (74.43), and **Jackson Merrill** (74.20). **Andy Pages** is particularly intriguing; while his base projection is solid, the combination of a favorable park and Eduardo Rodriguez\u2019s slow delivery suggests a high probability of a stolen base, an essential factor given our aggressive pursuit of the SB category. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) also warrants attention, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Grant Holmes provides the highest floor among our mid-tier hitters.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Wade Meckler** (48.08), who narrowly missed the cut behind lower-ranked but better-positioned starters. While **Wade Meckler** benefits from a lead-off spot, the optimizer favored the efficiency of **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** to maintain our positional coverage, despite their tougher matchups against Cam Schlittler and Emerson Hancock. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Drake Baldwin** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, both of whom face high-caliber arms with xERAs under 3.30. Should official lineups shift **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Jacob Wilson** from their projected spots, we may see a slight contraction in their efficiency scores, though they remain locked in to anchor the heart of the order.",
